              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The link you provided, **`http://www.rewardclub.me/`**, is highly suspicious and appears to be a **phishing or scam domain**. \n\n### Why this domain is highly suspicious:\n* **No Official Presence:** There is no legitimate, well-known company or loyalty program that officially uses `rewardclub.me` as their primary domain. \n* **Common Scam Format:** Scammers frequently register `.me`, `.top`, or other cheap, alternative domain extensions to masquerade as official \"Reward Clubs\" (such as pretending to be associated with CVS, Walgreens, Amazon, or major banks).\n* **No Web Footprint:** The domain has no legitimate search engine index or credible business registration, which is a classic hallmark of a temporary domain set up purely for phishing campaigns.\n\n### How these links are usually used (Smishing/Phishing):\nThese links are typically sent via unsolicited text messages (SMS \"smishing\") or emails. The messages often try to create a false sense of urgency by claiming:\n* *\"Your loyalty points are about to expire. Redeem them now.\"*\n* *\"You have been selected to receive a $100/250 gift card. Click here to claim it.\"*\n* *\"A package is waiting for you, but we need to verify your rewards account.\"*\n\nOnce you click the link, it will usually direct you to a fake login portal designed to steal your username, password, or credit card information.\n\n### What you should do:\n1. **Do not click the link.** If you have already clicked it but did not enter any information, close the tab immediately. \n2. **Never enter personal info.** Do not type in your name, phone number, address, passwords, or credit card details.\n3. **Verify directly:** If you believe a company actually wants to give you rewards, do not use the link in the message. Instead, open a new browser tab, go to the official website of the company (e.g., typing `cvs.com` or `target.com` manually), and log into your account there.\n4. **If you already entered information:** \n   * **Passwords:** If you entered a password that you use for other accounts, change those passwords immediately.\n   * **Financial Info:** If you entered credit card details, contact your bank or credit card provider right away to freeze or cancel the card.",
